        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="1272" n="1121" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v07-09mSupp/pg1121"/>

                <head>283. Memorandum from Col. Legere to Col. Ewell, January 16<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d283-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-01-16">January 16, 1963</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d283-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d283-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Tactical Nuclear Study</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. This morning Carl Kaysen gave me the
                    attached draft memo from himself to Gilpatric and amplified upon it orally. He has recently spoken
                    with some high-level people in Defense, and they agree with his feeling that by
                    1 March it will be impossible for the Special Studies Group to turn out a
                    definitive paper which might at least tend to silence the skeptics on one side
                    or both of the argument. I might add right here that he is not dead sure he will
                    send the attached draft, but has asked me for suggestions in modifying it.</p>
                <p>2. I believe Kaysen’s thinking, as known
                    to you, comes through quite clearly in the attached draft. Just to nail it down,
                    he expressly told me that Alain Enthoven
                    wonders why Pershings cannot do everything the shorter-range stuff can. In
                    short, the command and control tail is wagging the nuclear dog. However, the
                    idea of extending the study deadline may be a good one; Kaysen notes in this connection that General
                        Taylor would probably go along—with
                    the understanding that the decisions on production for FY 65 would also be delayed and would not be pre-judged.</p>
                <p>3. I would recommend holding my contacts with Kaysen on a sensitive basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Legere</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d283-a1.xml" xpointer="d283-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
